+### Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+|---|---|---|
+| `VITE_API_URL` | _(required)_ | Backend API base URL |
+| `VITE_SUFFIX` | `''` | URL path prefix for the app |
+| `VITE_ALLOWED_IMAGE_DOMAINS` | `''` | Trusted external image domains (see below) |
+
+#### VITE_ALLOWED_IMAGE_DOMAINS
+
+Controls which external image domains are rendered in LLM/assistant markdown output. Images from domains not on the list are replaced with a "blocked" badge, preventing data exfiltration via image requests to attacker-controlled servers.
+
+- **Format:** Comma-separated list of hostnames. A leading dot (`.example.com`) allows the apex domain and all its subdomains. Each entry must have at least two labels (e.g. `example.com`, not `com`).
+- **Default (empty):** All external images are blocked. Same-origin and backend-origin images are always allowed regardless of this setting.
+- **Example:** `cdn.example.com,.trusted.org,images.partner.io`
+
+```env
+# Block all external images (default — recommended for air-gapped deployments)
+VITE_ALLOWED_IMAGE_DOMAINS=
+
+# Allow a CDN and all subdomains of a partner domain
+VITE_ALLOWED_IMAGE_DOMAINS=cdn.example.com,.trusted.org
+```
+
+In Kubernetes deployments, set `viteAllowedImageDomains` in `deploy-templates/values.yaml`.
+
